      "description": "China is set to host the 33rd APEC Economic Leaders' Meeting next week in its high-tech Shenzhen city, where the presidents of China, the US and Russia will hold a historic trilateral summit.\nThe meeting of the 21-nation Asia-Pacific Economic Cooperation (APEC) Economic Leaders will take place November 18-19.\nIt gains importance as Chinese President Xi Jinping will host a summit with his US and Russian counterparts, Donald Trump and Vladimir Putin. Discussions at the trilateral summit are expected to focus on a host of global issues, including global conflicts, AI and the reduction of nuclear weapons by big powers.\nThe White House confirmed that the three leaders are planning to meet on the sidelines of a summit in China next week.\nThe historic meeting between the leaders of the US, Russia and China will take place as Trump attends the APEC summit in Shenzhen, White House spokeswoman Olivia Wales told the media.\n\"The president has made it clear that, among other topics, he will ..",
